Patch 2912: two-thread drawing, PIPE=1 (default off; experiment). After the PIPE work of another v19 port.

render_frame is split into render_frame_prepare (stays on the FIFO thread: GPU wait, shader and pipeline work, texture
uploads, descriptor writes, everything that reads guest memory or live state) and render_frame_submit (draw loop, post
passes, Close/Execute, Present). With PIPE=1 the submit half runs on its own thread for batch N while the FIFO thread
records batch N+1 into the other draw list (s_draws_buf[2]) and the other half of every upload ring. RfFrame carries the
batch (list, count, parity, present flag, MVP snapshot); rf_detach hands it over and resets the per-batch state;
pipe_wait (delivers sent window messages while waiting) runs before the next prepare, before a VS slot is reused, before
the base VS is built and at shutdown. Debug switches that read records or guest memory from the submit half keep the old
path.

J-Stars specific: the draw loop looked the pipeline up again (vp_get_fp_pso hashes the fragment program in guest memory
at that moment) and patch 2058 filled the fragment constants there too. On the submit thread the game has moved on by
then (first try: pipelines 1280, [FPA] queue full storm, cyan picture, 2 flips/s). With PIPE=1 the prepare half keeps
the pipeline and "still building" in the record (pso_pre, pso_pend) and fills the constants; the submit half uses them.
PIPE off: the old path, unchanged.

Tested (Experiments workbench, all-CPU 2 vs 2 on Hidden Leaf at 4K, SHADOW_SCALE=4, MODEL_DETAIL=4, SMAA): PIPE off 24.16,
27.17; PIPE=1 23.41, 25.41, 24.18 flips/s (fights differ run to run); picture correct; [PIPE] FIFO thread waits 0.10-0.17 ms
per batch. No gain by itself in this fight: the game thread and the FIFO thread take turns (sampling profile: FIFO thread
62% busy, 39% of its samples waiting), so the submit half was not the limit.

